    "a_defined_by_src": "No. Grep src/ returns 0 matches for 24 of them; the 25th (checkpoint_migrations) appears only in migrations.py.",
    "b_shared_library_out_of_scope": true,
    "b_rationale": "These 25 tables reside in the public schema of the shared PostgreSQL database 'langgraph'. 7 are langgraph library tables (agent_events/agent_runs/agent_schema_version/agent_thread_activity = langgraph Agent; checkpoint_migrations/store/store_migrations = langgraph-checkpoint-postgres version+store). The remaining 18 (inbound_events/outbox_events/it_assets/knowledge_chunks/knowledge_documents/routing_rules/satisfaction_surveys/sla_policies/support_members/support_schedules/support_teams/tenant_it_policies/ticket_assignments/ticket_messages/ticket_sla/ticket_status_events/ticket_workflow_runs/tickets) belong to a DIFFERENT support/ticketing/ITSM/knowledge domain application sharing the same DB. None are this e-commerce after-sales refund system's data-plane tables (which are tenants/memberships/sessions/operations/approvals/executions/streams/stream_events/audit/checkpoint_thread_scopes + checkpoints/checkpoint_blobs/checkpoint_writes).",
    "b_does_not_affect_12_table_rls_conclusion": true,
    "c_gap_fail_for_this_system": false,
    "c_rationale": "Since none of the 25 are this system's tenant data-plane tables, they are NOT tables that this system 'should have applied RLS to'. Accordingly there is no GAP and no FAIL against this acceptance's data-plane RLS scope.",
    "note_checkpoint_migrations": "checkpoint_migrations is created by this repo's initialize_checkpoint_schema (mirroring langgraph-checkpoint-postgres MIGRATIONS). Because it is a library version-tracking table (single 'v' column) with no tenant_id and no tenant data, applying RLS to it is neither required nor meaningful; it is classified as shared-library bookkeeping, not a GAP.",
    "observation_over_broad_grant": "INFO (not a failure of this scope): this repo's apply_runtime_role executes 'GRANT SELECT,INSERT,UPDATE,DELETE ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA public TO app_runtime', which granted app_runtime DML on ALL 38 public tables INCLUDING these 25 shared non-RLS tables (confirmed in pg_rls_policies.json app_runtime_table_grants / app_runtime_dml_grants). Because those tables are not RLS-enforced and app_runtime holds DML on them, this is a cross-tenant/data-exposure hardening consideration for a future task. It does NOT invalidate the 12-table data-plane RLS verification (that used app_runtime on the 12 RLS tables, correctly filtered)."
